Subject: [PATCH] Make the frontend VFS opt-in instead of unconditional

Kodi's game.libretro wrapper answers RETRO_ENVIRONMENT_GET_VFS_INTERFACE for
every core and only uses the addon.xml property supports_vfs for its own
load-time consistency check. FBNeo therefore routes all archive I/O through
the frontend handle, and a seek through that handle fails: unzOpen() aborts
and the core logs "No romset found at ...", so every zipped set refuses to
load. The core's own stdio parses the same archives without a problem.

Gate the VFS initialization behind FBNEO_FRONTEND_VFS so a frontend that
hands out a working interface can still enable it, while a plain build keeps
its own file I/O.

diff --git a/src/burner/libretro/libretro.cpp b/src/burner/libretro/libretro.cpp
index 28c115e..0a46ae4 100644
--- a/src/burner/libretro/libretro.cpp
+++ b/src/burner/libretro/libretro.cpp
@@ -370,12 +370,19 @@ void retro_set_environment(retro_environment_t cb)
 	struct retro_vfs_interface_info vfs_iface_info;
 	vfs_iface_info.required_interface_version = FILESTREAM_REQUIRED_VFS_VERSION;
 	vfs_iface_info.iface                      = NULL;
+#ifdef FBNEO_FRONTEND_VFS
 	if (environ_cb(RETRO_ENVIRONMENT_GET_VFS_INTERFACE, &vfs_iface_info))
 	{
 		dirent_vfs_init(&vfs_iface_info);
 		filestream_vfs_init(&vfs_iface_info);
 		path_vfs_init(&vfs_iface_info);
 	}
+#else
+	/* Frontend VFS is opt-in: a frontend that offers an interface without
+	   supporting it breaks archive parsing here (a seek through the handle
+	   fails and unzOpen() aborts), so the core keeps its own stdio. */
+	(void)vfs_iface_info;
+#endif
 
 	struct retro_core_options_update_display_callback update_display_cb;
 	update_display_cb.callback = apply_dipswitches_from_variables;
